; ============================================================
; TITLE:    POLYSPI Slideshow
; CATEGORY: Classic Logo
; LEVEL:    Beginner
; TAGS:     turtle geometry, spirals, recursion, color
; SUMMARY:  POLYSPI from Turtle Geometry grows the side a little each step, and a slideshow shows what different angles do.
; ============================================================
;
; WHAT IT DOES
;   Shows a slideshow of spirals. Each one is drawn by POLYSPI with a
;   different angle: 90 makes a square spiral, 91 makes it twist,
;   120 makes a triangle spiral, 144 a star spiral, and so on.
;
; HOW TO USE
;   Press Run and watch. Afterwards type your own, for example
;   clean polyspi 2 117 3  in the command center.
;
; CONCEPTS YOU WILL LEARN
;   * a recursive procedure that changes one of its inputs
;   * a stop rule (the base case) so the recursion ends
;   * FOREACH to run the same thing for every item of a list
;
; THINGS TO TRY
;   * Add 89 and 92 to the list of angles. Which way do they twist?
;   * Change the increment from 3 to 1 for a finer spiral.
;   * Make the stop size bigger than 300 and see the turtle leave the window.
; ============================================================

; Abelson and diSessa's Turtle Geometry (1981) builds POLYSPI from POLY
; by letting the side grow:
;     TO POLYSPI :SIDE :ANGLE :INC
;       FORWARD :SIDE  RIGHT :ANGLE
;       POLYSPI (:SIDE + :INC) :ANGLE :INC
;     END
; Like POLY it never stops on its own. We add one line at the top, a
; stop rule, so the spiral ends when the sides get long.

to polyspi :side :angle :inc
  if :side > 300 [stop]
  ; The color depends on the side, so the spiral fades from the
  ; middle outwards through the rainbow.
  setpencolor (list 255 - :side / 2 (:side * 3) / 4 + 40 120 + :side / 3)
  forward :side
  right :angle
  polyspi :side + :inc :angle :inc
end

; One slide: start in the middle, draw, write the angle, then pause
; so the picture can be enjoyed.
to slide :angle
  clean
  penup home pendown
  polyspi 2 :angle 3
  penup
  setxy -380 -280
  setheading 0
  setpencolor 7
  label (sentence [polyspi 2] :angle 3)
  wait 90
end

clearscreen hideturtle
setbackground [15 15 30]
setpensize 2
setlabelheight 20
foreach [90 91 120 121 144 72 60 175] [slide ?]
